{{!
    @template mod_playerpuzzle/giveup_dialog

    The confirmation that comes before giving up a match, a native <dialog> opened from the stage's flag button.
    It is moved inside the game's container when the game boots, so it also shows in full screen.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title - The dialog's title
    * text - What giving up costs
    * confirmlabel - The button that gives up
    * cancellabel - The button that goes back to the match

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Give up the match?",
        "text": "This counts as a defeat: one attempt is spent and the coins earned in this phase are lost.",
        "confirmlabel": "Give up",
        "cancellabel": "Keep playing"
    }
}}
<dialog id="playerpuzzle-giveup" class="pp-giveup" aria-labelledby="pp-giveup-title" aria-describedby="pp-giveup-text">
    <h2 id="pp-giveup-title" class="pp-giveup-title">{{title}}</h2>
    <p id="pp-giveup-text">{{text}}</p>
    <div class="pp-giveup-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" id="pp-giveup-confirm">{{confirmlabel}}</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="pp-giveup-cancel" autofocus>{{cancellabel}}</button>
    </div>
</dialog>
